lessons.notes:
## if, else if, else

```cpp
if (score >= 90) {
    grade = 'A';
} else if (score >= 80) {
    grade = 'B';
} else {
    grade = 'C';
}
```

## Operators

| Kind | Operators |
|------|-----------|
| comparison | `==` `!=` `<` `<=` `>` `>=` |
| logical | `&&` `\|\|` `!` (or `and`, `or`, `not`) |

Logical operators short-circuit: `b != 0 && a / b > 1` never divides by zero.

## if with initializer (C++17)

```cpp
if (int r = n % 3; r == 0) {
    std::cout << "divisible by 3\n";
}
```
`r` exists only inside the `if`/`else`.

## switch

```cpp
switch (day) {
    case 6:
    case 7:
        std::cout << "weekend\n";
        break;
    default:
        std::cout << "weekday\n";
}
```
Works with integers, `char` and `enum`s. Mark intentional fall-through with `[[fallthrough]];`.

## Ternary

```cpp
int biggest = (a > b) ? a : b;
```

## Common bugs

- `if (x = 5)` assigns instead of comparing.
- Missing `break` in a switch.
- Comparing doubles with `==`: use a small tolerance instead.

